  "known_boundaries": [
    "Compiler-core acceptance still executes five functions per mode; 100 emitted and linked rows do not imply 100 executed functions.",
    "Mandatory normalization precedes generic x86-64 selection. Optional instruction-form rewrites still use recursive selection; ordinary CLI selection retains its explicit selector option.",
    "Structured adapter envelopes carry validated deferred preparation recipes; transporting the envelope does not itself run optimization or produce optimized LLVM IR.",
    "Vector PHIs, stack-passed or oversized vectors, general wide-memory and wide-ABI shapes, indirect-branch PHI edges, and assembly or layouts outside checked envelopes remain unsupported.",
    "The bounded checked i128 constant multiply does not admit general i128 products.",
    "Execution depends on LLVM IR construction, the pinned Zig linker and compiler-rt, libc/CRT and single-threaded startup. No self-hosting or optimization-performance claim is made."
  ],
  "prior_failures": [
    "The first full run stopped at gate 8 when structured IR-writer optimization was rejected. The retained failed run precedes the shared adapter preparation repair.",
    "Prepared recipe execution exposed incorrect descriptor slice behavior, missing typed records/declarations, calling convention and TLS mismatches, FP literal bitcasts, array addressing and a false-success Base64 matcher. The frozen full run validates their repairs.",
    "LLVM and AddressSanitizer independently validate all 24 corrected Base64 recipes. Earlier focused failures remain in local-state.",
    "The second full run stopped at Fibonacci Safe compilation under the default 120-second command deadline. An isolated reproduction records timed_out, return code 124 and actual termination -15. The manifest now grants 900000 ms to compilation and owner replay; executable observations retain their 5000 ms deadline."
  ],
  "next_milestone": "Add diverse unchanged programs and more callable compiler-core functions through shared semantic and register repairs.",
